n the immediate d5. Though d5 was a "safer" alternative to a clear small advantage. this line also threatens discoveries on the queen and completes black's developement. . } 19. d5 (19. Qc1 d5)) 18. Bb3 { [%eval -0.88] } g5 { [%eval -0.59] } 19. Be5 { [%eval -0.99] } Nxe5 { [%eval -1.07] } 20. Nfxe5 { [%eval -0.74] } Be6 { [%eval -0.55] } 21. Kh1?! { [%eval -1.63] } { Inaccuracy. a5 was best. } (21. a5 Qxa5 22. Nxc6 Qb5 23. Nde5 Nd6 24. Qd3 Rac8 25. Qxb5 Nxb5 26. c3 f6) 21... f6 { [%eval -1.23] } 22. Nf3 { [%eval -1.15] } Bf7 { [%eval -1.2] } 23. Qc1 { [%eval -1.15] } Bg6 { [%eval -1.27] } 24. g4?! { [%eval -1.94] } { Inaccuracy. Ba2 was best. } (24. Ba2 a5 25. c4 Rad8 26. Re3 Bf8 27. Bb1 Re6 28. cxd5 cxd5 29. Nc5 Bxc5) 24... Kh7 { [%eval -1.8] } 25. Nf2?! { [%eval -2.69] } { Inaccuracy. Ba2 was best. } (25. Ba2 Qb7 26. c4 Qd7 27. cxd5 cxd5 28. Nc5 Qxg4 29. Bxd5 Rac8 30. Qc4 Nxc5) 25... Nxf2+ { [%eval -2.63] } 26. Rxf2 { [%eval -2.56] } Be4 { [%eval -2.65] } 27. Rd1?! { [%eval -4.16] } { Inaccuracy. Qd1 was best. } (27. Qd1 f5 28. Kg1 Bxf3 29. Rxf3 Rxe1+ 30. Qxe1 Qxd4+ 31. Kf1 Qxg4 32. Re3 Qf4+) (27. a5 Qxd4) 27... f5 { [%eval -3.89] } 28. a5 { [%eval -4.06] } Qb4 { [%eval -3.68] } 29. h3?! { [%eval -4.9] } { Inaccuracy. Kg1 was best. } (29. Kg1 Bxf3 30. Rxf3 fxg4 31. Rfd3 Re2 32. R1d2 Rae8 33. Rxe2 Rxe2 34. Kf1 Rxh2) 29... fxg4 { [%eval -5.34] } 30. hxg4 { [%eval -5.12] } Rf8 { [%eval -5.22] } (30... Re7) 31. Kg2 { [%eval -5.2] } Rf4 { [%eval -5.11] } 32. Kg3?! { [%eval -7.42] } { Inaccuracy. Re1 was best. } (32. Re1 Qxd4 33. Qxf4 gxf4 34. Rfe2 Qb4 35. g5 Rf8 36. Kh2 Kh8 37. Nh4 f3) 32... Raf8 { [%eval -7.15] } 33. Rdf1 { [%eval -7.9] } Qd6 { [%eval -8.63] } 34. Nxg5+ { [%eval -8.23] } hxg5 { [%eval -8.34] } 35. Rxf4 { [%eval -8.17] } gxf4+ { [%eval -7.78] } 36. Rxf4? { [%eval #-8] } { Checkmate is now unavoidable. Kf2 was best. } (36. Kf2 Bxd4+ 37. Ke2 f3+ 38. Kd1 Qh2 39. Qd2 Qg2 40. Qxg2 fxg2 41. Rxf8 g1=Q+) 36... Bh6 { [%eval #-7] } { 0-1 Black wins. } (36... Bf